      "rust_file": "src/hook.rs",
      "rust_item": "fn[dispatch_plugin_hooks]",
      "text": [
        "/// Dispatch plugin hooks with format routing.",
        "///",
        "/// Accumulates output as `serde_json::Value` in the host agent's wire format.",
        "/// When a plugin's format matches the host agent, input/output pass through directly.",
        "/// When formats differ, conversion goes through symposium canonical types.",
        "/// `prior_context` is the context already in `prior_output`; every hook's",
        "/// context is added to it (see [`JoinedContext`]).",
        "///",
        "/// Returns `Ok(json)` on success, `Err(stderr)` on exit code 2.",
        "#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.hook_gating`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.native_input`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.native_output`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.canonical_input`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.canonical_output`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.raw_json_fallback`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.hook_stdin_payload`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.merge_later_wins`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.joined_context`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.deny_final`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.exit_2_stops`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.hooks.best_effort`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.consent.unconsented_inactive`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.consent.consented_active`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.consent.dormant_inactive`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.consent.use_wakes_dormant`",
        "// {impl}`design.requirements.consent.offline_resolution`",
        "pub async fn dispatch_plugin_hooks(",
        "    sym: &Symposium,",
        "    host_agent: HookAgent,",
        "    event: HookEvent,",
        "    sym_input: &symposium::InputEvent,",
        "    original_input: &str,",
        "    prior_output: serde_json::Value,",
        "    prior_context: Option<String>,",
        "    deps: &Arc<Workspace>,",
        ") -> Result<serde_json::Value, Vec<u8>> {",
        "    let workspace = deps.info().await.cloned();",
        "    let registry = crate::plugins::load_registry_with_workspace(sym, workspace.as_ref()).await;",
        "",
        "    // Resolving the workspace means running cargo, so only do it when some",
        "    // plugin's hook gating references a concrete crate (a `depends-on(*)`",
        "    // wildcard or env/shell/path predicate never needs the crate graph), or",
        "    // when there is crate-plugin expansion to perform — that too evaluates",
        "    // predicates against the crate graph.",
        "    let dep_ids = if hook_dispatch_needs_deps(sym, &registry.plugins) {",
        "        deps.dep_ids().await.to_vec()",
        "    } else {",
        "        Vec::new()",
        "    };",
        "    let pms = deps.pms();",
        "    let used = workspace",
        "        .as_ref()",
        "        .map(|ws| crate::discovery::used_plugins(sym, pms, &registry.plugins, &ws.root))",
        "        .unwrap_or_default();",
        "    let mut ctx = crate::predicate::PredicateContext::new(&dep_ids).with_used(&used);",
        "    // Dispatch over the active set — registry plugins plus crate-sourced ones —",
        "    // so a crate plugin's hooks fire exactly like a registry plugin's.",
        "    let plugins = crate::plugins::active_plugins(",
        "        sym,",
        "        &registry,",
        "        pms,",
        "        workspace.as_ref().map(|ws| ws.root.as_path()),",
        "        &mut ctx,",
        "        symposium_install::UpdateLevel::None,",
        "    )",
        "    .await;",
        "    let hooks = dispatched_hooks_for_payload(&plugins, sym_input, host_agent, &mut ctx);",
        "",
        "    let mut output = prior_output;",
        "    let mut context = JoinedContext::new(event, prior_context);",
        "",
        "    for hook in hooks {",
        "        tracing::info!(",
        "            plugin = %hook.plugin_name,",
        "            hook = %hook.hook_name,",
        "            format = ?hook.format,",
        "            \"running plugin hook\"",
        "        );",
        "",
        "        // Determine stdin for the plugin based on its declared format.",
        "        // After format selection, the only two cases are:",
        "        // - native (matches host agent) → the agent's own payload, byte for byte",
        "        // - symposium → deliver canonical format",
        "        let hook_agent = hook.format.as_agent();",
        "        let stdin_str = if hook_agent == Some(host_agent) {",
        "            original_input.to_string()",
        "        } else {",
        "            match AgentHookInput::to_string(sym_input) {",
        "                Ok(s) => s,",
        "                Err(e) => {",
        "                    tracing::error!(plugin = %hook.plugin_name, hook = %hook.hook_name, error = %e, \"failed to serialize hook input\");",
        "                    continue;",
        "                }",
        "            }",
        "        };",
        "",
        "        let spawn_res = match build_spawn_spec(sym, &hook).await {",
        "            Ok(spec) => spawn_from_spec(spec),",
        "            Err(e) => {",
        "                tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"failed to prepare hook command\");",
        "                continue;",
        "            }",
        "        };",
        "",
        "        match spawn_res {",
        "            Ok(mut child) => {",
        "                if let Some(mut stdin) = child.stdin.take() {",
        "                    let _ = stdin.write_all(stdin_str.as_bytes());",
        "                }",
        "",
        "                let child_out = match child.wait_with_output() {",
        "                    Ok(o) => o,",
        "                    Err(e) => {",
        "                        tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"failed waiting for hook process\");",
        "                        continue;",
        "                    }",
        "                };",
        "",
        "                tracing::trace!(?child_out, \"hook finished\");",
        "",
        "                let exit_code = child_out.status.code();",
        "                tracing::debug!(",
        "                    report = %crate::report::ReportEvent::HookDispatched {",
        "                        plugin: hook.plugin_name.clone(),",
        "                        hook: hook.hook_name.clone(),",
        "                        exit_code,",
        "                        error: None,",
        "                    },",
        "                );",
        "                match exit_code {",
        "                    None | Some(2) => return Err(child_out.stderr),",
        "                    Some(0) if child_out.stdout.is_empty() => continue,",
        "                    Some(0) => {",
        "                        // Parse output and convert to host agent format.",
        "                        // Two cases: native (same as host) or symposium.",
        "                        let host_handler = crate::hook_schema::agent_event(host_agent, event);",
        "                        let Some(host_h) = host_handler else { continue };",
        "",
        "                        let (host_json, hook_output) = if hook_agent == Some(host_agent) {",
        "                            // Native format — parse as host agent output",
        "                            match host_h.parse_output(&child_out.stdout) {",
        "                                Ok(o) => (o.to_hook_output(), Some(o.to_symposium())),",
        "                                Err(e) => {",
        "                                    tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"failed to parse hook output\");",
        "                                    continue;",
        "                                }",
        "                            }",
        "                        } else {",
        "                            // Symposium format — parse and convert to host agent",
        "                            match serde_json::from_slice::<serde_json::Value>(&child_out.stdout) {",
        "                                Ok(v) => {",
        "                                    if let Ok(sym_out) =",
        "                                        serde_json::from_value::<symposium::OutputEvent>(v.clone())",
        "                                    {",
        "                                        let host_out = host_h.translate_output(&sym_out);",
        "                                        (host_out.to_hook_output(), Some(sym_out))",
        "                                    } else if v.is_object() {",
        "                                        (v, None)",
        "                                    } else {",
        "                                        tracing::warn!(",
        "                                            \"hook output is neither an output event nor a JSON object\"",
        "                                        );",
        "                                        continue;",
        "                                    }",
        "                                }",
        "                                Err(e) => {",
        "                                    tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"failed to parse hook output\");",
        "                                    continue;",
        "                                }",
        "                            }",
        "                        };",
        "",
        "                        merge(&mut output, host_json);",
        "                        if hook_output.as_ref().is_some_and(denies) {",
        "                            tracing::info!(",
        "                                plugin = %hook.plugin_name,",
        "                                hook = %hook.hook_name,",
        "                                \"plugin hook denied the tool call; later hooks do not run\"",
        "                            );",
        "                            return Ok(output);",
        "                        }",
        "                        context.add(hook_output.as_ref(), &mut output, host_h.as_ref());",
        "                    }",
        "                    Some(code) => {",
        "                        tracing::warn!(",
        "                            exit_code = code,",
        "                            \"plugin hook exited with non-zero (continuing)\"",
        "                        );",
        "                    }",
        "                }",
        "            }",
        "            Err(e) => {",
        "                tracing::debug!(",
        "                    report = %crate::report::ReportEvent::HookDispatched {",
        "                        plugin: hook.plugin_name.clone(),",
        "                        hook: hook.hook_name.clone(),",
        "                        exit_code: None,",
        "                        error: Some(e.to_string()),",
        "                    },",
        "                );",
        "                tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"failed to spawn hook command\");",
        "            }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    Ok(output)",
        "}"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "**Implementation.** In `dispatch_plugin_hooks` (src/hook.rs) every plugin hook is spawned with stderr piped (`spawn_from_spec`), and after `wait_with_output` the match on the exit status sends `None | Some(2)` (a block by exit status, including a hook killed by a signal) to `return Err(child_out.stderr)`, so the first blocking hook's raw stderr bytes leave dispatch and no later hook runs. `execute_hook` maps that `Err(stderr)` to `blocked_response(handler, event, &stderr)`, the only consumer. `blocked_response` decodes the bytes with `String::from_utf8_lossy` and trims surrounding whitespace to form the reason, then:\n\n- on `PreToolUse`, builds `PreToolUseOutput::deny(reason)` and translates it into the host agent's format, so the reason travels as `permissionDecisionReason` (Claude Code, Codex, Copilot), as `reason` (Antigravity), or as stderr with exit 2 (Kiro);\n- on every other event, returns `HookResponse::blocked(&reason)`, which is exit 2 with the reason as stderr; `run` writes `response.stderr` to the process's stderr and exits with `response.exit_code`.\n\n**Normalizations.** The reason is the hook's stderr text with leading and trailing whitespace trimmed (so `echo`'s trailing newline is dropped), and any bytes that are not UTF-8 are replaced with U+FFFD. Neither drops or replaces the hook's message. Both follow from the reason being carried as text (and in JSON on `PreToolUse`). When stderr is empty or only whitespace there is no stderr to give, and `blocked_response` substitutes `\"blocked by a plugin hook\"` instead. That case is specified by `hooks.block_reason_nonempty`.\n\n**Tests (all pass, run here).** In tests/hook_decisions.rs the fixture `plugin-hook-decisions0/.../scripts/block.sh` runs `echo 'blocked by the decisions plugin' >&2; exit 2`:\n- `plugin_exit_2_denies_the_tool_call_on_every_agent` checks that on `PreToolUse` every agent gets a denial carrying exactly that reason, through `assert_denied` (stdout JSON for Claude/Codex/Copilot/Antigravity, stderr plus exit 2 for Kiro);\n- `plugin_exit_2_on_a_prompt_passes_through` checks that on `UserPromptSubmit` every agent gets exit 2, empty stdout and exactly that reason on stderr;\n- `hook_command_exits_2_with_the_reason_on_stderr` runs the real `cargo agents hook` process and checks the exit status 2 and the stderr reason for Kiro `pre-tool-use` and Claude `user-prompt-submit`.\n\n**Limits.** The `PostToolUse`, `SessionStart` and `Stop` blocks, the no-exit-code (signal) case, and non-UTF-8 stderr are not tested. They are judged from the code, which runs the same `None | Some(2)` arm and the same non-`PreToolUse` branch of `blocked_response`. Whether an agent shows the reason it receives is that agent's behavior: Symposium always delivers it.\n\n**Refuted on review:** On every event other than `PreToolUse`, Antigravity is never given the reason. `blocked_response` returns `HookResponse::blocked(&reason)` there: exit 2, empty stdout, the reason only on stderr. Antigravity ignores exit codes and takes its outcome only from stdout (md/design/agent-details/antigravity-cli.md \"Exit Codes: Ignored. Exit 1 and exit 2 behave exactly as exit 0; only stdout decides the outcome\"; md/reference/agents/antigravity.md \"only what a hook writes to stdout affects the agent\"). `blocked_response`'s own doc comment cites this as the reason a `PreToolUse` block is translated into a stdout denial. Antigravity delivers `PostToolUse`, `PreInvocation` (`UserPromptSubmit`), `SessionStart` and `Stop`, so when a plugin hook on any of those exits 2 with \"X\" on stderr, `cargo agents hook antigravity <event>` exits 2 with empty stdout and \"X\" only on stderr. `plugin_exit_2_on_a_prompt_passes_through` asserts exactly this for Antigravity. Antigravity then treats the result as success and never receives \"X\" as a reason, even on `Stop`, where its stdout `{decision, reason}` would have carried one. The earlier claim that \"Symposium always delivers it\" equates writing to the process's stderr with giving the agent the reason. That does not hold for an agent that does not read stderr, and the code's own `PreToolUse` handling rejects the equation. The requirement holds for Claude Code, Codex and Kiro on every event and for every agent on `PreToolUse`. It is violated for Antigravity on its four other events.",
  "requirement": "When a plugin hook blocks by its exit status, Symposium MUST give the agent the hook's stderr as the reason."
}
